<title>USA: NY Nine Mile Point 2 nuke unit resumes full output.</title>
<headline>NY Nine Mile Point 2 nuke unit resumes full output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 1,137 megawatt (MW) Nine Mile Point 2 nuclear unit resumed full power production after being shut a week ago for repairs, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Thursday.</p>
<p>The adjacent 610 MW Nine Mile Point unit 1 was running at 82 percent of capacity during repairs on a circulation water pump, NRC said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>Niagara Mohawk Power Corp operates both Nine Mile Point generating units. It is the sole owner of unit 1 and 41 percent owner of unit 2.</p>
<p>New York State Electric and Gas Co and Long Island Lighting Co each hold 18 percent in unit 2, Rochester Gas and Electric Co 14 percent, and Central Hudson Gas and Electric Co nine percent.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
